From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:35:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7001-air2: Enable the speaker link

Set the NCO reference to the rate iBoot reports in a running J81's
Apple device tree (/arm-io clock-frequencies[10] = 342857142 Hz, 2.4 GHz
/ 7; the IPSW device tree leaves it 0), and enable the NCO, the
i2s-switch and MCA3 with its route from aud3 to pin3. No codec is
attached yet, so no sound card appears.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
index 1d33fef01..29e355181 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7001-air2.dtsi
@@ -198,6 +198,29 @@ &sio {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The NCO reference as iBoot reports it in a running J81's ADT
+ * (/arm-io clock-frequencies[10], the NCO's first clock-id 0x10a):
+ * 2.4 GHz / 7. iOS special-cases this rate for its divider precision.
+ */
+&nco_clkref {
+	clock-frequency = <342857142>;
+};
+
+&nco {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&i2s_switch {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/* The speaker link: MCA3 to pad 3 (ADT function-i2s_route aud3 -> pin3) */
+&mca3 {
+	apple,i2s-switch = <&i2s_switch 3 3>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &serial5 {
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart5_pins>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
-- 
2.56.0

